    <p>The other day, my daughter visited a zoo located close to Green Lake, Seattle. Later that day, she said she didn't see an elephant. That surprised me because, for me, an elephant or two are symbol for a zoo. That huge existence that is larger than any other walking-on-the-ground animals is overall a memorable experience of visiting a zoo. That massive poo of them are necessary sensary experience too.</p>
    <p>This baby elephan is cute. Babies of animals are cute because their relatively large eyes on their face occupy a large ratio of area on a face of an animal. Does anybody know an exsitence? Why do eyes play such an important role to impress others regardless of types of animals? We evenly see babies of any kinds of animals cute: elephants and humans.</p>
